Several things are at work.  Your WIS (WIS is the key stat for Hea,
Kni, Mon, Pri, Val, but I think INT still determines if you can learn
the spell or not).  Your divination spell skill (as a monk, you start
unskilled and can advance to basic).  Any metallic armor, shields
(even small shields, made of wood, will hinder spellcasting), or
gauntlets of power or fumbling will raise failure rates.

The biggest thing you need to do is to get to basic divination spell
skill.  Here are some wizmode tests:

Started with XL1 monk with WIS 9, read blessed spellbook of identify. 
Failure rate 88%.  #levelchange to 13, still 88% (hence, XL isn't
coming into play when you are unskilled).

Start quaffing blessed potions of enlightenment (to increase just INT
and WIS):

